We are to output the plan for the APPLY phase as a sequence of tool calls.

 We have decided on the following sequence:

  1. run_cmd('which authselect')
  2. run_cmd('authselect check')
  3. run_cmd('authselect enable-feature with-faillock')
  4. run_cmd('authselect apply-changes')
  5. run_cmd('read_file /etc/pam.d/password-auth')
  6. run_cmd('bash -c \'' 
        content="$1"; 
        if [[ ! "$content" =~ "pam_faillock.so preauth" ]]; then
            lines=($(echo "$content" | tr '\\n' '\\n')); 
            new_lines=(); 
            inserted=false; 
            for line in "${lines[@]}"; do
                stripped="$(echo "$line" | sed -e 's/^[[:space:]]*//')"; 
                if [[ ! $inserted && "$stripped" =~ ^auth && ! "$stripped" =~ ^# ]]; then
                    new_lines+=("auth        required      pam_faillock.so preauth"); 
                    inserted=true; 
                fi; 
                new_lines+=("$line"); 
            done; 
            if [[ ! $inserted ]]; then
                new_lines+=("auth        required      pam_faillock.so preauth"); 
            fi; 
            printf "%s\\n" "${new_lines[@]}"; 
        else
            echo "$1"; 
    \'')
  7. run_cmd('write_file /etc/pam.d/password-auth "$2"')

 However, note that the last two steps (6 and 7) are only executed if the authselect part fails (i.e., step 2 fails).

